@startuml state-machine
title Planner - avoidance manoeuvre (the /cmd_vel it publishes)

[*] --> Idle : boot

Idle : drive is false, nothing published
Cruise : linear.x = cruise_speed
Stop : zero command, stop_duration_s
Reverse : linear.x = -reverse_speed, reverse_duration_s
Turn : angular.z = turn_speed (counter-clockwise), turn_duration_s
Fault : zero command

Idle --> Cruise : drive set to true
Cruise --> Stop : range < stop_distance_m
Stop --> Reverse : after stop_duration_s
Reverse --> Turn : after reverse_duration_s
Turn --> Cruise : after turn_duration_s

Cruise --> Fault : range invalid or\nolder than range_stale_ms
Fault --> Cruise : valid fresh range

Cruise --> Idle : drive set to false
Stop --> Idle : drive set to false
Reverse --> Idle : drive set to false
Turn --> Idle : drive set to false

note right of Turn
  Stop, Reverse and Turn are one committed manoeuvre.
  The planner keeps to it on every step,
  whatever the range says, until it ends.
end note

note bottom of Cruise
  The controller applies its own limits on top
  (hard stop, blind stop, command heartbeat), whatever the command says.
end note

@enduml
